        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.782,
            0.104,
            0.899,
            0.12
          ],
          "content": "MATHEMATICS"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.141,
            0.595,
            0.269
          ],
          "content": "**Example 4 :** Mayank made a bird-bath for his garden in the shape of a cylinder with a hemispherical depression at one end (see Fig. 12.9). The height of the cylinder is 1.45 m and its radius is 30 cm. Find the total surface area of the bird-bath. (Take $\\pi   =   \\frac { 2 2 } { 7 } \\; )$"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.655,
            0.139,
            0.864,
            0.297
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_5_image_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.276,
            0.594,
            0.319
          ],
          "content": "**Solution :** Let h be height of the cylinder, and r the common radius of the cylinder and hemisphere. Then,"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.675,
            0.299,
            0.772,
            0.317
          ],
          "content": "Fig. 12.9"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.101,
            0.324,
            0.865,
            0.445
          ],
          "content": "the total surface area of the b $\\begin{aligned}\\mathrm{grid-batch} &= \\mathrm{CSA}   of   \\mathrm{cylinder} + \\mathrm{CSA}   of   \\mathrm{h} \\\\&= 2\\pi r h + 2\\pi r^2 = 2\\pi r(h + r) \\\\&= 2 \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times 30(145 + 30)   \\mathrm{cm}^2 \\\\&= 33000   \\mathrm{cm}^2 = 3.3   \\mathrm{m}^2\\end{aligned}$ hemisphere"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.402,
            0.468,
            0.595,
            0.487
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "EXERCISE 12.1"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.495,
            0.428,
            0.529
          ],
          "content": "Unless stated otherwise, take $\\pi = \\frac { 2 2 } { 7 } .$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.534,
            0.901,
            0.573
          ],
          "content": "**1.** 2 cubes each of volume 64 cm<sup>3</sup> are joined end to end. Find the surface area of the resulting cuboid."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.579,
            0.902,
            0.637
          ],
          "content": "**2.** A vessel is in the form of a hollow hemisphere mounted by a hollow cylinder. The diameter of the hemisphere is 14 cm and the total height of the vessel is 13 cm. Find the inner surface area of the vessel."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.645,
            0.9,
            0.684
          ],
          "content": "**3.** A toy is in the form of a cone of radius 3.5 cm mounted on a hemisphere of same radius. The total height of the toy is 15.5 cm. Find the total surface area of the toy."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.69,
            0.901,
            0.729
          ],
          "content": "**4.** A cubical block of side 7 cm is surmounted by a hemisphere. What is the greatest diameter the hemisphere can have? Find the surface area of the solid."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.735,
            0.902,
            0.793
          ],
          "content": "**5.** A hemispherical depression is cut out from one face of a cubical wooden block such that the diameter l of the hemisphere is equal to the edge of the cube. Determine the surface area of the remaining solid."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.801,
            0.534,
            0.899
          ],
          "content": "**6.** A medicine capsule is in the shape of a cylinder with two hemispheres stuck to each of its ends (see Fig. 12.10). The length of the entire capsule is 14 mm and the diameter of the capsule is 5 mm. Find its surface area."
        },
        {
